]","Sen. Cassidy, Bill [R-LA]","Sen. Cruz, Ted [R-TX]","Sen. Fischer, Deb [R-NE]","Sen. Graham, Darline [R-SC]"],"committees":[],"laws":[],"committeeReports":[],"costEstimates":[],"relatedBills":[{"title":"Protection of Women and Girls in Sports Act of 2021","relationship":"Cross-Congress related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/426"},{"title":"Protection of Women and Girls in Sports Act of 2021","relationship":"Cross-Congress related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/senate-bill/251"},{"title":"Protection of Women and Girls in Sports Act of 2023","relationship":"Cross-Congress related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/senate-bill/613"}],"textVersions":[{"date":"2025-01-08","stage":"Placed on Calendar Senate","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119s9pcs/xml/BILLS-119s9pcs.xml"}],"summaries":[{"date":"2025-01-07","stage":"Introduced in Senate","text":"Protection of Women and Girls in Sports Act of 2025\n\nThis bill generally prohibits school athletic programs from allowing individuals whose biological sex at birth was male to participate in programs that are for women or girls.\n\nSpecifically, the bill provides that it is a violation of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 for federally funded education programs or activities to operate, sponsor, or facilitate athletic programs or activities that allow individuals of the male sex to participate in programs or activities that are designated for women or girls. (Title IX prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex in federally funded education programs or activities, including in public elementary and secondary schools and in colleges and universities.) Under the bill, sex is based on an individual's reproductive biology and genetics at birth."}],"actions":[{"date":"2025-03-03","text":"Cloture on the motion to proceed to the measure not invoked in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 51 - 45. Record Vote Number: 100. (CR S1455-1456)"},{"date":"2025-03-03","text":"Motion to proceed to measure considered in Senate. (CR S1455)"},{"date":"2025-02-27","text":"Cloture motion on the motion to proceed to the measure presented in Senate. (CR S1434)"},{"date":"2025-02-27","text":"Motion to proceed to consideration of measure made in Senate."},{"date":"2025-01-08","text":"Read the second time. Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under General Orders. Calendar No. 2."},{"date":"2025-01-07","text":"Introduced in the Senate. Read the first time. Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under Read the First Time."},{"date":"2025-01-07","text":"Introduced in Senate"}]},"votes":[{"chamber":"Senate","congress":119,"session":1,"roll":100,"date":"2025-03-03","time":"06:27 PM","question":"On Cloture on the Motion to Proceed S. 9","description":"Motion to Invoke Cloture: Motion to Proceed to S. 9","result":"Cloture on the Motion to Proceed Rejected (51-45, 3/5 majority required)","amendment":"","amendmentDetail":"","tieBreaker":"","url":"https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00100.htm","xmlUrl":"https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00100.xml","counts":{"yes":51,"no":45,"present":0,"notVoting":4},"members":[{"id":"S428","name":"Alsobrooks, Angela","state":"MD","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","position":"no"},{"id":"S354","name":"Baldwin, Tammy","state":"WI","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","position":"no"},{"id":"S429","name":"Banks, Jim","state":"IN","party":"R","district":"","vote":"Yea","position":"yes"},{"id":"S317","name":"Barrasso, John","state":"WY","party":"R","district":"","vote":"Yea","position":"yes"},{"id":"S330","name":"Bennet, Michael","state":"CO","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","position":"no"},{"id":"S396","name":"Blackburn, Marsha","state":"TN","party":"R","district":"","vote":"Yea","position":"yes"},{"id":"S341","name":"Blumenthal, Richard","state":"CT","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","positi